        {
            "number": 2,
            "revision": "f52133066f4fd44d72d016f58c33ce6c482d82f2",
            "parents": [
                "3694fce9b0ce675d9c1d6cbefed7f8de9edf6227"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/98/85598/2",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                "username": "mox669"
            },
            "createdOn": 1764333023,
            "author": {
                "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                "username": "mox669"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Because we're opening pandoras box here, lets move toward the correct, typesafe APIs using operator/=.  I allowed these in in the first place because to_string on a uint64 is technically always representable as a dbus path for all values, and I didn't want to slow you guys down, but if we're going to go the route of technical correctness, we need to be using typesafe object_path objects.\n\nflushing these through std::format is one level too removed from being able to obviously see that these don't need escaped."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 831,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "sorry, i should have noted that earlier. Do you think this alternative would be better?\n\n\n```suggestion\n{\n    const sdbusplus::message::object_path settingsPath(std::format(\n        \"/xyz/openbmc_project/control/host{}/boot\",\n        computerSystemIndex));\n```\n\nFrom my perspective it is a tiny bit better since we have one less variable to go around.\n\nIf you agree with it that could be applied throughout the patch."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 831,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Don't have a strong opinion on that. Initially I went with what you are suggesting, but reverted to this, because I think it is a bit more readable. On the other hand we could have a couple less temporary variables. @ed@tanous.net any preference?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 831,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We should never be using std::format for constructing a dbus path because it doesn't escape or handle errors on bad input correctly, so both are wrong.\n\nCorrect here would be\n```\nsdbusplus::message::object_path settingsPath/xyz/openbmc_project/control);\nsettingsPath /= std::format(\"host{}\", computerSystemIndex);\nsettingsPath /= \"boot\";\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 831,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "btw, if someone wanted to go create an sdbupslus equivalent to boost::urls::format, or std::format, (something like sdbusplus::message::object_path::format()) that took the same arguments, that would be awesome, but until that exists, we continue to use the /= stuff."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 831,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "I agree that would be neat and a nice cpp side quest for cold winter days. Went with /= for now. Done"
                }
            ],
