                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 231,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Probably unrelated to this cleanup (so feel free to tell me to ask on a normal forum), but is this still needed?  I thought all daemons that were previously using Host had been moved to also expose Host0?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 231,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "You are right, they are also exposing Host0 (and Chassis0 for that matter) too.\n\n@patrick@stwcx.xyz noted on discord too, that the non-indexed service names have been deprecated and that he had a patch for bmcweb at some point. [1]\n\nI am not sure what exactly needs to be tested, but I created a follow-up patch where we can discuss that, if my testing isn't sufficient. [2] \n\nI tried to find a discussion / design doc that talks about the deprecation to reference it in the commit message, but haven't found any. So if I am overlooking something, I would appreciate it if you could point me into the right direction in the follow-up patch.   \n\n[1] https://discord.com/channels/775381525260664832/1385306077188460545\n[2] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/86030"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 258,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "going to have to explain this one to me.. This looks like the control path? \n\ngetHostControlObjectPath ?\n\ngetHostBootSettings ? \n\nIsn't there a /xyz/openbmc_project/settings ? And I would expect getSettingsObjectPath to go there"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 258,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "+1."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 258,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "I used 'Settings' here, because it comes from the 'Settings' dbus service and I thought it might be better suited. \n\nI overlooked '/xyz/openbmc_project/settings' though, thanks for pointing this out. \n\nUsing 'Control' and 'controlPath' now, to align with the other object path helper functions. Done"
                }
